::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. What is the topic of the speech? {
~A. Weather in the city.#Weather is not discussed. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=B. Public duty and citizenship.#Correct. The speech focuses on how citizens serve the city. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~C. Building materials.#The passage does not focus on construction. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~D. Travel across the city.#Travel is not discussed. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. What is the central idea? {
~A. Citizens should speak in the square every day.#The speech says service is not only speaking in the square. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~B. Laws are never useful.#The speech says laws cannot hold people together without responsibility, not that laws are useless.
=C. A city depends on citizens faithfully performing ordinary responsibilities.#Correct. This idea is developed across the speech. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~D. Children should never be taught.#The speech includes teaching truth as a positive duty. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. Which detail supports the central idea? {
~A. "speaking in the square"#This is mentioned, but the speech says duty is not only this. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~B. "Great laws"#This is part of the conclusion but not the clearest example. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~C. "the city"#This is the topic, not supporting evidence by itself. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=D. "returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth"#Correct. These examples show ordinary responsibilities. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
}

::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. How does the structure develop the central idea? {
