~D. It hides the main idea in unrelated details.#The details support the central idea. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. Which paraphrase is most accurate? {
~A. A city is honorable only when citizens make speeches.#This contradicts the speech. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~B. Small responsibilities do not matter if laws are strong.#This contradicts the final sentence. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~C. Citizens should avoid helping other people.#This contradicts the examples. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=D. The speech argues that everyday honest actions help hold a city together.#Correct. This paraphrase captures the central idea accurately. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
}
